   "gates": [],
   "blockers": [
    "part2.expect[1] (diagnosis and differentials), bullet 'Rotator cuff pathology or brachial neuritis': Brachial neuritis is grouped with rotator cuff pathology and argued against using full passive shoulder movement, pain below the elbow and reduced reflexes. None of these exclude brachial neuritis: it can cause a reduced biceps reflex, sensory change and normal passive shoulder range. This teaches wrong discriminating features, and item 30 is scored against this model answer. The ddx section has the right reasons.",
    "Checklist item 23 (sensation) together with the patient script exam findings 'Sensation' and the guide bullet on sensation: To earn the item the candidate must state pinprick, light touch, temperature, vibration and proprioception. But the examiner is told to stop the candidate as soon as they say they would examine sensation. A candidate who says 'I would now examine sensation' is cut off before naming the types and loses the item unfairly. The item also only says 'accepts' the finding; it never asks the candidate to identify it as C6, which is the point of the step."
